    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai\n\n### Description\n\nI'd like to have different mappings to go to the previous or next textobject. For now, mini.Ai only exposes the `goto_left` and `goto_right` options for movement. It would be nice to either have more options, for example relative to search methods:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\ngoto = {\r\n  next_or_cover = {\r\n    left = 'g[',\r\n    right = 'g]',\r\n  },\r\n  prev_or_cover = {\r\n    left = 'g(',\r\n    right = 'g)'\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe way I'd probably use it would be to map `next_or_cover.left` to `g]` and `prev_or_cover.right` to `g[`, given that I rarely think about which side of the textobject I'm in.\r\n\r\nAn alternative could be exposing directly the `expr_mapping` function, and allow users to make their own mappings while keeping the base options simpler.",
